      "statusChangeID": "6476045a8a071909276c66e1",
      "statusChangeNewStatus": "needs more information",
      "value": "Hi @{5f69f1c35688d0392edbcbb0|full_name}! I'm sorry to hear that you're not enjoying the software. What issues are you experiencing with the VCC?\n\nIf you have any bug reports or feature requests, feel free to submit an issue on GitHub: https://github.com/vrchat-community/creator-companion/issues/new/choose\n\nThe VRChat SDK can be installed without the VCC by following the manual installation steps here: https://vrchat.com/home/download\n\nNote that this may not give you access to community packages that rely on the VCC.\n\nIt's up to asset creators whether or not they'd like to publish their assets as `.unitypackage` files or as VCC listings. The VCC makes distributing and updating assets easier, so several creators prefer it.\n\nUsing the VCC should be as frictionless as possible. I'd appreciate your help with that!",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-05-27T17:47:19.628Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I dont like using VCC at all and i keep wanna add avatars and worlds to vrchat.\n\nThe program seems handy for new users but outside of that its pointless to me like giving me sand while walking in a desert.\n\nIm already having issues find assets cause most of them depend on VCC to be present and i cant use ANY of them cause vcc will NEVER be present.",
